# The one SDL2.dll the GUI uses on Windows (docs/contracts/cli/gui.md sections 2 and 6): the official libsdl-org
# release, by exact URL, verified by SHA-256 before anything is extracted. Never fetch it unpinned, never cache it.
# The hash is the one GitHub shows for the release asset (API field digest) and equals the SHA-256 of a download
# over TLS from this URL. Changing the version means changing both lines in one reviewed PR.
# Trust on first use: libsdl-org signs only the source archives of a release (SDL2-<version>.tar.gz.sig and .zip.sig),
# not the win32-x64 binary zip, so there is no upstream signature to check for this asset (checked for 2.32.10). When
# bumping, look again; if a signature for the binary zip appears, verify it and note the key fingerprint here.
url=https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL/releases/download/release-2.32.10/SDL2-2.32.10-win32-x64.zip
sha256=6cf9706eefd0a4a06dc764007934d428afaf029fabdd408a9e646048c91e18fb
